\<!-- ephemeral -->

# Rust Assist — List page `<entity.name>`

Use the exact generated `Q::<entity.rustPluralName>_minimal()` entry point.
Apply only model-derived filters and projections, a deterministic ID tie-breaker,
and the runtime's trusted materialization ceiling. Do not accept raw dynamic
query JSON or let a client override the hard limit.

```rust
use teaql_core::SmartList;
use <entity.domain.rustModuleName>::{
    Q, <entity.rustStructName>, TeaqlRuntime,
};

pub async fn list_<entity.rustModuleName>_page(
    context: &impl TeaqlRuntime,
    offset: u64,
    limit: u64,
) -> Result\<SmartList\<<entity.rustStructName>>, Box\<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    let page = Q::<entity.rustPluralName>_minimal()
<entity.fields:{f | <if(f.id)><else><if(f.version)><else><if(f.objectProperty)><else>        .select_<f.rustMemberName>()
<endif><endif><endif>}><entity.fields:{f | <if(f.objectProperty)>        .select_<f.rustMemberName>_with(Q::<f.fieldType.refer.rustPluralName>_minimal())
<endif>}><entity.rustOneToOneRelations:{r |         .select_<r.rustMemberName>()
}><entity.rustOneToManyRelations:{r |         .select_<r.rustMemberName>()
}><entity.fields:{f | <if(f.candidateForConst)>        .<f.rustAttributePredicatePrefixExpr>_is_<first(f.candidateForConst).rustCandidateMethodValue>()
<endif>}>        .order_by_id_asc()
        .comment("what: load a stable page of <entity.name> rows")
        .purpose("why: serve the authorized bounded <entity.name> list")
        .execute_for_page(context, offset, limit)
        .await?;

    Ok(page)
}
```

Request field-level Assist before adding or changing a field predicate. Boolean
field Assist documents the distinct `true`, `false`, `unknown`, and `known`
states without expanding every field vocabulary into this entity overview.

Compile the source unchanged. Prove exact filtering, projection and relation
selection, stable non-overlapping pages, filtered total count, enforcement of
the default 10,000-row hard limit, intent checks, and compilation failure for
unknown fields or client-controlled hard-limit APIs.

